ds the declared coordinator threshold and window: a non-positive, out-of-range or malformed threshold is off and a malformed window reads as the default. read_occupancy reads the newest valid assistant usage after the live transcript branch's latest compaction boundary, never a sidechain record, counting input and cached input; a record whose usage is malformed, partial or zero is skipped, and no valid usage reads as unknown, never zero. A primary-checkout lease names one coordinator session and its transcript. take refuses another holder; release frees the lease and clear unlatches it, each requiring and recording the owner's reason; hand_back accepts only the holder session and a handoff carrying a session prompt, frees the lease, and records the handoff; it refuses another or unnamed caller, whatever handoff it names, while naming the owner's release; it refuses the holder's own pending relaunch request, while a previous holder's request does not block it and is left for session_end's foreign-request refusal; with the guard off it returns before reading or writing. Elapsed time never transfers ownership. on_session_start installs a session as holder, unlatched, only when it presents the successor token the holder's exit wrote into the lease, and restates a latched drain to the holder's own resumed start. Only the holder's own hook payload on the holder's transcript is measured, never a subagent's. latch_reading latches drain when the unrounded reading reaches the threshold and retains it through lower readings, compaction and resume; it ends only through the owner's clear, the owner's release, the holder's hand-back, or a successor take. window_refusal runs before the dial on every claim route, including the dispatcher, naming the UTC end; the dispatcher remains exempt only from the context guard. claim_refusal identifies the claimant by the session id the agent CLI exports to its tool processes (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID), refuses with no lease held or a claimant that is not the holder, and reads and latches the holder's transcript itself, so a refusal never depends on a hook having run; a claim holding the dispatch lock never calls it. While a window is armed hooks act at every dial and deny the closed list of the main session's Agent call, SendMessage call, Bash/PowerShell model-CLI command word, and a Bash/PowerShell line unreadable only because of an unclosed single quote, unclosed double quote, unclosed POSIX dollar quote, unclosed POSIX backtick substitution, unclosed dollar-parenthesis substitution, or unclosed PowerShell here-string. One quote-aware shell reading per dialect reads quoted values as the shell does, and treats quoted separators, comments and here-document and here-string bodies as data. It finds the model-CLI command word after leading variable assignments, the timeout and env prefixes, the shell's reserved words, the chain operators and the call operator, and in substitutions written in the line or inside double quotes. It reads a PowerShell assignment to a variable as running its right-hand command, while a quoted or variable right-hand value stays data. A form outside this list gets no dedicated recognition: it may incidentally match this reading, and carries no guarantee either way. window_check exits nonzero inside an armed window. At every SessionStart inside a window, hooks inject the blackout close-down instruction; each main session's monitored events inject it at that session's first monitored event in the window and every twentieth thereafter, counted per session per window: bring each open lane to its pause point, using a wrap-up adjudication for an active claim where needed; write the handoff naming each lane and its next obligation; request no relaunch; and end the session. Hook responses inject the latch instruction once and bounded reminders thereafter; inside a blackout window the latch is still recorded, but the blackout close-down, which requests no relaunch, is injected in its place. PreCompact records trigger, occupancy and latch/request state; classify_compaction reports missed-threshold, manual and during-drain cases.\"","+code_symbol = \"GuardConfig/guard_config/Occupancy/read_occupancy/lease_dir/take/release/clear/hand_back/record_event/latch_reading/window_refusal/claim_refusal/on_blackout/launch_reason/model_clis/command_name/command_words/_assigned/window_check/on_monitored/on_session_start/on_pre_compact/classify_compaction/hook;claim;segments/Unreadable/Word\"","+detail = \"guard_config reads the declared coordinator threshold and window: a non-positive, out-of-range or malformed threshold is off and a malformed window reads as the default. read_occupancy reads the newest valid assistant usage after the live transcript branch's latest compaction boundary, never a sidechain record, counting input and cached input; a record whose usage is malformed, partial or zero is skipped, and no valid usage reads as unknown, never zero. A primary-checkout lease names one coordinator session and its transcript. take refuses another holder; release frees the lease and clear unlatches it, each requiring and recording the owner's reason; hand_back accepts only the holder session and a handoff carrying a session prompt, frees the lease, and records the handoff; it refuses another or unnamed caller, whatever handoff it names, while naming the owner's release; it refuses the holder's own pending relaunch request, while a previous holder's request does not block it and is left for session_end's foreign-request refusal; with the guard off it returns before reading or writing. Elapsed time never transfers ownership. on_session_start installs a session as holder, unlatched, only when it presents the successor token the holder's exit wrote into the lease, and restates a latched drain to the holder's own resumed start. Only the holder's own hook payload on the holder's transcript is measured, never a subagent's. latch_reading latches drain when the unrounded reading reaches the threshold and retains it through lower readings, compaction and resume; it ends only through the owner's clear, the owner's release, the holder's hand-back, or a successor take. window_refusal runs before the dial on every claim route, including the dispatcher, naming the UTC end; the dispatcher remains exempt only from the context guard. claim_refusal identifies the claimant by the session id the agent CLI exports to its tool processes (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID), refuses with no lease held or a claimant that is not the holder, and reads and latches the holder's transcript itself, so a refusal never depends on a hook having run; a claim holding the dispatch lock never calls it. While a window is armed hooks act at every dial and deny the closed list of the main session's Agent call, SendMessage call, Bash/PowerShell model-CLI command word, and a Bash/PowerShell line unreadable only because of an unclosed single quote, unclosed double quote, unclosed POSIX dollar quote, unclosed POSIX backtick substitution, unclosed dollar-parenthesis substitution, or unclosed PowerShell here-string. One quote-aware shell reading per dialect reads quoted values as the shell does, and treats quoted separators, comments and here-document and here-string bodies as data. It finds the model-CLI command word after leading variable assignments, the timeout and env prefixes, the shell's reserved words, the chain operators and the call operator, and in substitutions written in the line or inside double quotes. It reads a PowerShell assignment to a variable as running its right-hand command, while a quoted or variable right-hand value stays data. A form outside this list gets no dedicated recognition: it may incidentally match this reading, and carries no guarantee either way. window_check exits nonzero inside an armed window. At every SessionStart inside a window, hooks inject the blackout close-down instruction; each main session's monitored events inject it at that session's first monitored event in the window and every twentieth thereafter, counted per session per window: bring each open lane to its pause point, using a wrap-up adjudication for an active claim where needed; write the handoff naming each lane and its next obligation; request no relaunch; and end the session. Hook responses inject the latch instruction once and bounded reminders thereafter; inside a blackout window the latch is still recorded, but the blackout close-down, which requests no relaunch, is injected in its place. PreCompact records trigger, occupancy and latch/request state; classify_compaction reports missed-threshold, manual and during-drain cases. After identifying a session, the lease take first reads the guard hooks' state and records no holder unless it reads none or on, or a terminal consent installs them and the re-read reads on; without a terminal at absent, or at occupied, it refuses naming the consent step or the hooks to move.\""," rationale = \"The context reading and lease are one admission fact: without one holder and a latched record, a tool-event observation can be missed and a later claim can start new work after the coordinator should be closing out.\"","-test_refs = \"TC-315;TC-316;TC-317\"","+test_refs = \"TC-315;TC-316;TC-317;TC-345\""," status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6"]},{"oldStart":3436,"oldLines":11,"newStart":3436,"newLines":11,"lines":[" "," [design.LLR-322]"," sr_refs = [\"SR-032\"]","-title = \"Dev-setup consents to coordinator-hook opt-in\"","+title = \"Coordinator guard hooks are read by name and installed only with consent\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/dev-setup.template.sh;project-trajectory/scripts/dev-setup.template.ps1;scripts/dev-setup.sh;scripts/dev-setup.ps1;project-trajectory/scripts/coordinator_guard.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/guard_hooks.py\"","-code_symbol = \"offer_hooks/OfferHooks/Offer-Hooks;hooks_state/enable_hooks;guard_groups/bind/command_shapes/merged\"","-detail = \"When the shipped coordinator-hook example declares guard hooks and the machine-local settings leave them off, an interactive consent may enable them by merging the guard hooks into the machine-local settings, each command bound to the floor-resolved interpreter that runs the opt-in, replacing only the guard's own commands. A command is the guard's only when it has the exact shape the shipped example defines: an interpreter, either the example's own word or a bound absolute path, followed by the guard script and hook subcommand; every other command, including one that merely names the guard file, is preserved along with its group's configuration and unrelated settings, and a group is dropped only when no command remains. The committed project settings are never written and a re-run is idempotent. A declined offer changes neither configuration nor credentials, and an example with no guard hooks creates no settings change. In this repository the committed settings contain no guard group, the inert example declares every guard group the guard serves at the repository guard path, and developer setup reports the machine-local opt-in as on or off and, when off, where it is offered.\"","-rationale = \"Coordinator hooks change a contributor's interactive environment, so an explicit opt-in preserves existing configuration and leaves a declined setup reversible.\"","+code_symbol = \"offer_hooks/OfferHooks/Offer-Hooks;_hooks_admission/_terminal_ask/_is_terminal/_ask_on_stdout/_hooks_main;guard_groups/bind/read_state/is_guard_command/refusal_text/local_settings/hooks_state/install_hooks/consent_install\"","+detail = \"The guard hooks' state over the shipped example and the machine-local settings is one of none, absent, on or occupied, with each guard event checked by the guard's command name. A missing machine-local file, or all missing guard events, is absent; a parsed null is occupied. At absent, the developer-setup offer and the lease take each install the example's guard groups only after a terminal yes. At a terminal, the shared consent question is displayed before its answer is read. The install is bound to the running interpreter and keeps every other key and event, and each route goes on only when a re-read reads on. Without a terminal, the lease take refuses and names the consent step; on Windows, a character device that is not a console is no terminal. At occupied, every route writes nothing and names the file, events, commands and fix. If a consented install fails or re-reads other than on, the lease take refuses without recording a holder; its refusal names the file, error and fix, and the developer-setup offer reports that refusal as missing. A failed reader is reported missing, never none. No re-enable path exists. In this repository, the committed settings contain no guard group, the inert example declares every guard group the guard serves at the repository guard path, and developer setup reports the state and, when absent, where it is offered.\"","+rationale = \"Coordinator hooks change a contributor's interactive environment, so an explicit opt-in leaves a declined setup reversible.\""," test_refs = \"TC-345\""," status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-009\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-927\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3508,"oldLines":13,"newStart":3508,"newLines":13,"lines":[" phase = 6"," "," [test.TC-345]","-verifies = [\"SR-032\", \"LLR-322\"]","+verifies = [\"SR-032\", \"LLR-322\", \"SR-229\", \"SR-237\", \"LLR-300\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"Decline and accept the interactive coordinator-hook offer with existing settings, and run the hook command against examples with and without guard hooks. Run an installed hook with a real Python below the floor first on PATH, where one is installed, and check the scaffold's git ignore list. Inspect this repository's committed settings and its inert example, then run this repository's developer-setup readiness report on both supported families.\"","+method = \"Read the four states over the Trust shapes; drive the consented install at the developer-setup offer and lease take, in-process, through a pseudo-terminal, and at a Windows console; confirm that the terminal displays the shared question before its answer; run the failed-write, reader-failure, no-guard and older-Python cases.\""," tier = \"Smoke\"","-expected = \"Consent enables the coordinator hooks in the machine-local settings, bound to the opt-in's interpreter, replacing only the guard's own commands defined by the shipped example's command shape, so a user command sharing a group with a guard command, including one that names the guard file, keeps its place and its group's matcher, and an older bare-python guard command is replaced by the bound one; a re-run changes nothing; an installed hook still denies with an older Python first on PATH; the machine-local file is git-ignored; denial changes no configuration or credential; and an example without guard hooks changes nothing. This repository's committed settings contain no guard group, its inert example carries every served guard group at the repository guard path, and its readiness report names the opt-in as on or off with the offer location.\"","+expected = \"The state is none, absent, on or occupied according to the guard events' command names. A missing machine-local file, or all missing guard events, is absent; a parsed null is occupied. At a terminal, the shared consent question is displayed before its answer is read. At absent, terminal consent at the developer-setup offer and the lease take installs the example's guard groups into the machine-local settings, bound to the running interpreter while retaining other keys and events, and each route continues only after a re-read is on. Without a terminal, including on Windows a character device that is not a console, the lease take refuses without recording a holder and names the consent step. At occupied, every route writes nothing and names the file, events, commands and fix. A failed reader is reported missing, never none. An example with no guard group changes nothing, and no re-enable path is available. The committed settings contain no guard group; the inert example declares every served group at the repository guard path; and the developer-setup report names the state and, when absent, the offer location. A failed consented install refuses the lease take without recording a holder and names the file, error and fix; the developer-setup offer reports that refusal as missing.\""," automated = \"Yes\"","-evidence = \"tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_denial_changes_no_configuration_or_credential; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_hooks_command_reports_and_switches_on; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_hook_opt_in_merges_and_keeps_existing_hooks; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_hook_opt_in_with_no_guard_hooks_changes_nothing; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_an_installed_hook_denies_with_an_older_python_first; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_scaffold_keeps_the_machine_local_settings_out_of_git; tests/test_coordinator_guard.py::test_the_guard_hooks_are_this_repos_opt_in_not_its_tracked_settings; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_this_repos_readiness_report_names_the_hooks_opt_in\"","+evidence = \"tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_denial_changes_no_configuration_or_credential; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_hooks_command_reports_each_state_and_writes_nothing; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_user_command_beside_the_guards_reads_occupied_and_nothing_is_written; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_each_occupied_shape_refuses_and_writes_nothing; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_hooks_command_refuses_enable; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_an_absent_install_binds_every_group_and_keeps_other_keys; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_declined_or_empty_or_eof_answer_writes_nothing_and_asks_again; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_an_on_file_is_left_byte_for_byte_and_nothing_is_asked; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_hook_opt_in_with_no_guard_hooks_changes_nothing; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_an_installed_hook_denies_with_an_older_python_first; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_scaffold_keeps_the_machine_local_settings_out_of_git; tests/test_coordinator_guard.py::test_the_guard_hooks_are_this_repos_opt_in_not_its_tracked_settings; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_this_repos_readiness_report_names_the_hooks_opt_in; tests/test_coordinator_guard.py::test_the_hooks_reading_is_none_absent_on_or_occupied; tests/test_coordinator_guard.py::test_a_user_command_ending_in_the_guards_name_reads_as_the_guards; tests/test_coordinator_guard.py::test_guard_hooks_holds_no_merge_or_ownership_code; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_failing_or_silent_hooks_reader_is_reported_missing_never_none; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_at_a_terminal_a_yes_installs_every_guard_group_keeping_other_keys; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_at_a_windows_console_a_yes_installs_every_guard_group_keeping_other_keys; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_an_on_file_is_unchanged_and_not_offered_at_a_terminal; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_an_occupied_slot_is_reported_and_never_offered; tests/test_coordinator_guard.py::test_with_the_hooks_absent_and_no_terminal_the_take_refuses_naming_dev_setup; tests/test_coordinator_guard_e2e.py::test_the_cli_take_with_the_hooks_absent_and_no_terminal_refuses; tests/test_coordinator_guard.py::test_the_take_goes_on_at_on_and_at_none; tests/test_coordinator_guard.py::test_an_occupied_slot_refuses_the_take; tests/test_coordinator_guard.py::test_at_a_terminal_the_take_asks_installs_and_takes_after_a_yes_and_refuses_after_a_no; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_cli_take_at_a_pseudo_terminal_asks_and_installs; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_cli_take_at_a_windows_console_asks_and_installs; tests/test_coordinator_guard.py::test_a_consented_install_whose_write_fails_refuses_the_take; tests/test_coordinator_guard.py::test_a_failed_offer_names_the_file_the_error_and_the_fix; tests/test_coordinator_guard.py::test_a_stdin_on_the_null_device_is_no_terminal; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_at_a_windows_console_a_failed_install_names_the_file_error_and_fix; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_at_a_real_terminal_a_failed_install_names_the_file_error_and_fix\""," status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-927\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-927\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-927\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-927\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BiKHnTrRopjEtp7EjekQ5C","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
